---
// src/pages/projects.astro
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Projects">
  
  <section style="margin-bottom: 4rem;">
    <div class="project-data-header comic-panel">
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 8vw, 3.5rem); text-align: center; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Project Data</h1>
      <p style="text-align: center; font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 3vw, 1.1rem); color: var(--color-secondary); font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase;">
        Deployed infrastructure, predictive modeling, and live web architecture.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="comic-panel" style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.2rem); border-bottom: 4px solid var(--color-black); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Personal ML & Full-Stack</h2>
      
      <div class="project-grid">
        
        <div class="project-card">
          <div class="project-header">
            <h3>NBA Finals NLP Predictor</h3>
            <span class="status live">Live on Streamlit</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pill-container">
            <span class="pill-tag">Python</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">NLP</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Whisper</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">RAG</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Streamlit</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Sentiment Analysis</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            An end-to-end NLP pipeline tracking team momentum through postgame media sentiment. I built this to process live-scraped press conference data, scrubbing out broadcast noise to keep the dataset accurate. It features a custom Whisper audio-transcription fallback and a RAG pipeline that allows users to query team dynamics, providing evidence-based predictions for the 2026 NBA playoffs.
          </p>
          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="https://nba-finals-predictor-2026-izrjrrysjipdqjlrqbv5z7.streamlit.app/" target="_blank" class="comic-btn mini-btn">View App</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/ishansinha5/NBA-Finals-Predictor-2026" target="_blank" class="comic-btn mini-btn secondary-btn">View GitHub Repository</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card">
          <div class="project-header">
            <h3>OpticHash (Distributed Edge-Vision Pipeline)</h3>
            <span class="status live">Live Deploy</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pill-container">
            <span class="pill-tag">Microservices</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Python/FastAPI</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">JavaScript/Vercel</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">C++</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">pHash</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Previously a standard web application, I am refactoring the architecture into a compute-optimized microservices pipeline. My focus is on architectural integrity—using a C++ perceptual hashing layer to intercept duplicate images and a Python FastAPI backend to run vision inference only when necessary. This drastically reduces GPU compute load and improves data processing efficiency.
          </p>
          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="https://optichash.vercel.app/" target="_blank" class="comic-btn mini-btn">Live Deploy</a>
            <a href="https://github.com/ishansinha5/Optichash" target="_blank" class="comic-btn mini-btn secondary-btn">View GitHub Repository</a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="comic-panel">
      <h2 style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 5vw, 2.2rem); border-bottom: 4px solid var(--color-black); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Academic & Computational</h2>
      
      <div class="project-grid">
        
        <div class="project-card">
          <div class="project-header">
            <h3>NFL Combine Predictive Analysis</h3>
            <span class="status">Python / ML</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pill-container">
            <span class="pill-tag">Python</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Machine Learning</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Random Forest & SVM</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Academic Project</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            This started as an academic project and grew into a supervised machine learning suite. I used Random Forest and SVM ensembles to predict NFL rookie trajectories, evaluating draft classes for the NFC North and a few other key teams.
          </p>
          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="https://github.com/ishansinha5/NFL-Combine-Predictive-Analysis" target="_blank" class="comic-btn mini-btn secondary-btn">View GitHub Repository</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="project-card">
          <div class="project-header">
            <h3>ISS Telemetry Analytics</h3>
            <span class="status">Computational Modeling</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pill-container">
            <span class="pill-tag">Python</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Data Visualization</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Unsupervised Learning</span>
            <span class="pill-tag">Academic Project</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Built as an extension of my CMSE coursework, this is an unsupervised learning and spatial analysis pipeline. I mapped orbital bias and altitude decay by processing telemetry data streams to calculate structural limits and optimize trajectory models.
          </p>
          <div class="project-links">
            <a href="https://github.com/ishansinha5/ISS-Telemetry-Analytics" target="_blank" class="comic-btn mini-btn secondary-btn">View GitHub Repository</a>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>

  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .project-data-header {
    background-color: var(--color-panel);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-black);
    box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px var(--color-black);
    padding: clamp(1.2rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .project-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .project-card {
    background-color: var(--color-panel);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-black);
    padding: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 1.5rem);
    box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px rgba(11, 9, 10, 0.1);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease;
  }

  .project-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-4px) translateX(-4px);
    box-shadow: 10px 10px 0px rgba(11, 9, 10, 0.15);
  }

  .project-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .project-header h3 {
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 1.6rem);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .pill-container {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .pill-tag {
    background-color: var(--color-white);
    border: 2px solid var(--color-black);
    color: var(--color-black);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 20px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.5px;
  }

  .status {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--color-black);
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .status.live {
    background-color: #2A9D8F; 
    color: var(--color-white);
  }

  .status.dev {
    background-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .project-card p {
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 3vw, 1rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .project-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .mini-btn {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    padding: 0.4rem 1rem;
    border-width: 3px;
    box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px var(--color-black);
  }

  .mini-btn:active {
    transform: translate(4px, 4px);
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px var(--color-black);
  }

  .secondary-btn {
    background-color: var(--color-bg);
  }
  .secondary-btn:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-secondary);
  }
</style>